<article class="env-lemma" id="09IG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09IG">Lemma <span data-tag="09IG">10.120.18</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian domain of dimension $1$ with fraction field $K$. Let $L/K$ be a finite extension. Let $B$ be the integral closure of $A$ in $L$. Then $B$ is a Dedekind domain and $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ is surjective, has finite fibres, and induces finite residue field extensions. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Krull-Akizuki (Lemma <a href="/tag/00PG" data-tag="00PG">10.119.12</a>) the ring $B$ is Noetherian. By Lemma <a href="/tag/00OK" data-tag="00OK">10.112.4</a> $\dim (B) = 1$. Thus $B$ is a Dedekind domain by Lemma <a href="/tag/034X" data-tag="034X">10.120.17</a>. Surjectivity of the map on spectra follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/00GQ" data-tag="00GQ">10.36.17</a>. The last two statements follow from Lemma <a href="/tag/031F" data-tag="031F">10.119.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>